  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-navigator-javaenabled gives javaEnabled as an attribute that returns true depending on whether or not Java is enabled.\n\nIn Chrome and Firefox at least, it is actually a method. [Gecko comments indicate](https://github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev/blob/d14fba3fa1d2182ae44b2cf659047434723fff1f/dom/webidl/Navigator.webidl#L208) everyone supports it that way.\n\n[Gecko still does actual Java-enabled checks](https://github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev/blob/c4f40f5dfcbfb637735cf96cc2c834c1ac3ab8c2/dom/base/Navigator.cpp#L711). Blink [always returns false](https://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/modules/plugins/NavigatorPlugins.cpp&q=JavaEnabled&sq=package:chromium&type=cs&l=61) but I guess that is accurate since Java is never enabled in Blink anymore. Although it returns true in stable for me.\n\nSo probably the action item here is to just to change it to a method instead of a property.\n",
